memo-rag (0.12.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename Debian source/binary package from "memo" to "memo-rag"
    to avoid silent collision with Debian's unrelated note-taking
    "memo" package (apt was upgrading installs to memo 1.7.x).
  * Add Conflicts: memo and Replaces: memo (<< 1.0~) so existing
    trans/memo 0.x installs upgrade cleanly and Debian's memo is
    blocked at install time.
  * Doc dir moves to /usr/share/doc/memo-rag/.
  * Binary names (/usr/bin/memo, /usr/bin/memo-arcana), config
    paths (/etc/memo/), system user, and systemd unit are unchanged.

 -- trans <trans@github.com>  Fri, 08 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

memo (0.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add ${VAR} expansion in namespaces.yaml from process env
  * Split config: memo.env (defaults) + secrets.env (deployment-managed)
  * Add /usr/share/doc/memo/secrets.env.example
  * Secure /etc/memo directory (750 root:memo)
  * Default ARCANA_PORT=19118

 -- trans <trans@github.com>  Sat, 12 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

memo (0.11.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Multi-namespace routing: memo-arcana now supports isolated
    embedding spaces per namespace. Each `ns` has its own DB,
    USearch index, and embedding provider.
  * New actions: open, close, list.
  * Config via /etc/memo/namespaces.yaml with preload support.
  * Memo system user no longer has a home directory.

 -- trans <trans@github.com>  Sat, 12 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

